WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.667
(elegant music)

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.997
- [Interviewer] A quote from
Director Darren Aronofsky,

00:00:12.997 --> 00:00:14.430
"One of my very first calls

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.470
was to my makeup artist, Adrien Morot,

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.470
'Can we do something that's
incredibly realistic?'"

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:20.760
- No pressure.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.470
That's the first thing. (chuckles)

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:25.350
And then the next thing he said
is that, "Well, by the way,

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.460
we're gonna see him nude.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.020
He's gonna have short sleeves.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.520
He's gonna have short pants."

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.054
And we ended up having 12
weeks to build a makeup.

00:00:32.054 --> 00:00:34.530
(elegant music)

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:38.280
- What a great chance to create
these two iconic characters,

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.770
well, one iconic character
and then the villain.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.500
And then, really, the other
bit was Elvis's progression.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.410
You know, the more Tom Parker
got his claws into Elvis,

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.840
it manifested in the way he looked

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.480
right through where he
sings "Unchained Melody"

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.523
several weeks before he passed away.

00:00:54.544 --> 00:00:55.530
- [All] Yes!

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.000
- Every day was like,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.520
I started in the night and
I finished in the night.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.430
We had like 200 soldiers every day,

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:06.900
everyone with like wigs or
facial hair, dirt, teeth,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.690
because we didn't want it to
have the white teeth anymore,

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.880
then marching to set,

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.470
basically to the battlefield (chuckling).

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:16.680
And what you have seen in front of camera,

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.950
it looked the same behind
the camera. (chuckling)

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.800
- Hey, bitches!
(machine gun reporting)

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.420
- [Interviewer] Certainly
one of the standout makeups

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.010
in the movie is The Penguin.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:26.940
It's not a makeup.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.100
It's a complete and utter transformation

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.240
of Colin Farrell.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.400
- I looked at it at a
different perspective.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.750
Matt Reeves had some ideas

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.090
about how he was a little bit like Fredo

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.020
from "The Godfather."

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.320
I said, "How can I incorporate
a Penguin in here?"

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.810
- I felt like it was kind of a culmination

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:45.120
of all the makeups that
Mike and I have done

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.846
and really using almost
every trick in the book.

00:01:47.846 --> 00:01:50.596
(dramatic music)

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.890
- This movie was all about the women.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:58.230
You see, there's very few men
in it actually, (chuckles)

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.630
and it's about their connection.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:03.600
One of the main things that I
think about "Wakanda Forever"

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.360
is that it's a franchise
that could have been over,

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.100
because we lost our star.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.090
What kind of movie gets a chance
to come back as a rebirth,

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.470
and we got that opportunity.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.270
And that's the most beautiful thing.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.567
(elegant music)

